From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:52:50 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 188/207] dsv41: map abstain anchors onto the fields the client
 gets, after tool parsing

T5's r10 review blocked 7f32fcd28: the map was taken before openai.attachCalls cut
tool envelopes (an anchor 10 that should be 61) and from a lossy decode (U+FFFD
made 14 bytes look like 12).

- runner_projection.runtimeOf maps at serialization: on the whole message after
  attachCalls and the strips, or on the chunks the stream actually sent (Sent).
- rawFields rebuilds the raw fields from tokenBytes, as runner_text.zig counts
  the runner's anchors; no token bytes means no map.
- mapOf maps the final field as one raw run after a blank head, or after any
  head when the final bytes occur once; otherwise (a lossy decode, a cut) null.
- A raw anchor below 0 or past raw_bytes leaves its field unmapped.

(cherry picked from commit 2e0e7a0f2b080c68e444f6d522a6fbde13727096)
